    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6348A\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the social services law, in relation to authorizing and\ndirecting county public welfare districts to accept paperwork electron-\nically\n\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the social services law, in relation to authorizing and\ndirecting county public welfare districts to accept paperwork electron-\nically\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo make the electronic submission process implemented during the COVID-\n19 pandemic permanent, eliminating the unnecessary requirement for\nsocial service beneficiaries to travel to submit routine paperwork, and\nstreamlining the administrative process for County DSS offices.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Provides that each county commissioner of public welfare is\nauthorized and directed to ensure that their public welfare district\nprovides individuals with the mechanism to submit their public assist-\nance paperwork remotely.\n\nSection 2: Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDuring the COVID-19 pandemic, beneficiaries of County Department of\nSocial Services were allowed to submit paperwork remotely instead of\nhaving to travel into the office each time they needed to submit a\nsimple form. Counties saw paperwork compliance rates go up, while bene-\nficiaries were able to save time and travel expenses getting to County\noffices, often a large burden. This bill would make this practice perma-\nnent, eliminating the unnecessary requirement for social service benefi-\nciaries to travel to submit routine paperwork, and streamlining the\nadministrative process for County DSS offices.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPACT:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
